PROBE 0 — Demo Descriptions (text-only)
============================================================
  Probe 0 response:
Demo 1:
- Key physical principle: Rotational hinge mechanism allowing the window to swing outward.
- Sequence of actions: Turn the handle partway to unlock or release the window, then push the window outward on its side hinge until it swings open about 90 degrees.

Demo 2:
- Key physical principle: Lever mechanism controlling the recline angle of the armchair backrest.
- Sequence of actions: Pull the recline lever to the first click to tilt the backrest about 30 degrees; attempt to pull to the second click is blocked by the wall, so return to the first position.

Demo 3:
- Key physical principle: Sliding mechanism along a horizontal track.
- Sequence of actions: Grip the window frame firmly and push it sideways along the track to slide the window smoothly to the right, opening the left side.

Demo 4:
- Key physical principle: Crank and scissor arm mechanism converting rotational motion into linear extension.
- Sequence of actions: Turn the rotating crank handle clockwise, causing the scissor arm to extend and push the window outward from the bottom edge.

